WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.535
-Whenever Donald Trump
holds a press conference,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.936
his rambling nonsensical answers

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.471
raise more questions
than they answer.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:08.040
So we decided to hold another
one right here, right now.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.509
That's right. Donald Trump,
and the "Late Night" Press Corps

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:11.978
are here in our studio
and ready to go.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.446
So without further ado,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:16.315
it's time for the "Late Night"
White House press conference.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.352 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:24.090
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.160
-Mr. President, Mr. President,
Mr. President, Mr. President.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.328
Mr. President, yes, thank you.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.229
Seth Meyers,
"Late Night with Seth Meyers."

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:34.233
President Trump, how would you
describe the current state

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.701
of your presidency?

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.104
-In the final couple of weeks.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.005
-Oh.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:41.607
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:45.078
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.446
-Mr. President, what would
you say to Mike Pence,

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:49.949
who was probably hoping
that you'd be impeached by now,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.216
and he'd be the president?

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:52.519
-Too bad, Mike.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.820
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.723
-How long have you been
president?

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.892
-For like 44 years or something.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.227
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:04.029
-I haven't seen Jared Kushner
in a while. Where is he?

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:05.932
-Being held hostage...

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.234
in Venezuela.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.936
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:13.339
-Hey, did you hear that my wife
and I had a second child?

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.975
-Congratulations. I'm sure
you're very unhappy about that.

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:21.514
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.183
-You bragged that when you ran
the Miss Universe Pageant,

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.119
you used to barge into
the dressing room.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.287
What did you do when
you went in there?

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.089
-I'd say, come on,
let me see what you have.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:34.393
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.262
-What do you tell your barber?

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.263
-Make it look like not good.

00:01:38.263 --> 00:01:40.333
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.873
-Hey, how's Melania?

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:50.143
-I don't know if she likes me
anymore, but that's okay.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.777
She used to.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:54.847
-What do you see when you
stand on the bathroom scale?

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.849
-Large, large numbers.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.053
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:04.390
-What's the hardest part
about having a threesome?

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.692
-You can't do them
simultaneously, by the way.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.194
Just think if somebody said,
"Oh, you can do them both."

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.362
No, you can't. Because
if they're doing that,

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:11.698
we're not doing the other.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:16.969
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:19.205
-What's between your ears?

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.173
-Beautiful, perfect air.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:24.277
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:27.547
-Can you tell me what words

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.448
would you use
to describe yourself?

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.885
An ignorant, narcissistic,
racist?

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.485
-Those words. Those exact words.

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:38.958
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.627
-How often do you have
an empathetic human thought?

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.963
-Averaging one per decade.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.398
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:48.834
-Every time I make biscuits --
you know when you make biscuits?

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.604
Well, when I make biscuits,
they turn out really dry.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.272
What should I do?

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:55.041
-Speak to Mr. Pillsbury.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.777
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:05.150
-Important question here --
how many children do you have?

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.153
-It looks like three.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.054
Could be four.

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:10.790
Perhaps it could be two.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.191
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.726
-Is that your final answer?

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.528
-Two, or one, or three.

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:17.863
-You're almost there.

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.832
-One, or two, or three,
or four, or five.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.633
[ Ding! ]
-Hey, you got it!

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:26.238
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:29.642
And finally, I'd like to finish

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.077
with the same question
I always ask.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.611
President Trump,
how's your penis?

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.047
-It'll never hold up.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.982
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.116
-How's your penis?

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:40.152
-Little, almost not at all.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:41.420
-And how is your penis?

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.222
-That's such a racist question.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:44.256
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:45.892
-Okay, then how's your penis?

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.560
-Pretty nasty
to be honest with you.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.596
-Well, looks like
we're out of time.

